## 1. CI workflow

| Field | Value | Citation file:line |
|---|---|---|
| CI triggers | Pull requests, pushes to `main`, and manual dispatch. | [`.github/workflows/ci.yml`](../../../.github/workflows/ci.yml#L1-L6) |
| Offline environment | Ubuntu 24.04 runner with a pinned pgvector/PostgreSQL service and disposable CI credentials. | [`.github/workflows/ci.yml`](../../../.github/workflows/ci.yml#L50-L65) |
| Offline contracts | Documentation, dataset, live-E2E, notebook, JavaScript, unit/pgvector/HTTP, deployment, image packaging, and HTTPS checks run in the offline job. | [`.github/workflows/ci.yml`](../../../.github/workflows/ci.yml#L70-L194) |
| Headroom artifact | The job checks artifact SHA, sample counts, saturation, tool hook and raw P99 values against a 50 ms SLO. | [`.github/workflows/ci.yml`](../../../.github/workflows/ci.yml#L97-L166) |
| Colab compatibility | Python 3.13 checks the agent notebook, dependencies, protocol and tool contract. | [`.github/workflows/ci.yml`](../../../.github/workflows/ci.yml#L13-L49) |
